no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:15.545 --> 00:13:19.174
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:20.116 --> 00:13:22.516
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:22.686 --> 00:13:25.280
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:25.455 --> 00:13:28.322
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:28.492 --> 00:13:29.516
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:29.693 --> 00:13:32.253
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:32.429 --> 00:13:34.363
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:34.531 --> 00:13:37.557
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:37.734 --> 00:13:39.759
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:39.936 --> 00:13:41.904
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:42.072 --> 00:13:43.096
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:43.273 --> 00:13:47.141
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:50.711
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:50.881 --> 00:13:53.975
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.448
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:58.554
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:58.722 --> 00:14:00.952
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:01.124 --> 00:14:04.321
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:04.494 --> 00:14:08.760
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:08.932 --> 00:14:10.900
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:11.401 --> 00:14:14.928
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:17.474 --> 00:14:22.912
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:23.079 --> 00:14:25.639
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:25.815 --> 00:14:27.908
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:28.084 --> 00:14:29.813
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:29.986 --> 00:14:32.614
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:32.789 --> 00:14:36.122
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:36.293 --> 00:14:37.920
Again.


00:14:38.094 --> 00:14:39.652
Really? Okay.


00:14:39.829 --> 00:14:45.461
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:45.635 --> 00:14:46.761
Ouch.


00:14:46.937 --> 00:14:49.997
I could belch the song better.


00:14:51.608 --> 00:14:53.769
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:53.944 --> 00:14:55.411
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:55.579 --> 00:14:58.480
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:58.648 --> 00:15:02.550
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:02.919 --> 00:15:06.582
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:10.794 --> 00:15:13.160
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.059
No.


00:15:15.231 --> 00:15:17.529
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:29.713 --> 00:15:33.012
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:33.183 --> 00:15:35.651
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:46.129 --> 00:15:49.223
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:54.104 --> 00:15:55.833
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:56.006 --> 00:15:57.098
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:57.273 --> 00:16:01.369
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:01.544 --> 00:16:02.875
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:03.046 --> 00:16:05.810
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:06.249 --> 00:16:07.546
Victor!


00:16:07.717 --> 00:16:10.948
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:11.121 --> 00:16:13.282
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:16.793 --> 00:16:18.420
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:28.338 --> 00:16:29.498
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:29.673 --> 00:16:31.072
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:31.241 --> 00:16:34.677
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:34.844 --> 00:16:36.505
Crap.


00:16:39.916 --> 00:16:41.611
This is insane.


00:16:41.785 --> 00:16:45.846
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:55.632 --> 00:16:57.725
You gotta be kidding me.


00:16:59.469 --> 00:17:01.096
Crap.


00:17:04.407 --> 00:17:08.002
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:08.178 --> 00:17:11.978
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:12.148 --> 00:17:14.275
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:14.451 --> 00:17:16.146
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:16.319 --> 00:17:18.879
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:19.055 --> 00:17:22.115
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:22.292 --> 00:17:24.522
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:24.694 --> 00:17:26.821
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:29.165 --> 00:17:30.632
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:36.806 --> 00:17:38.671
Victor.


00:17:42.512 --> 00:17:43.945
Katie?


00:17:45.148 --> 00:17:47.378
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:47.584 --> 00:17:50.849
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:53.784
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:54.824 --> 00:17:56.655
The truth. Um...


00:17:57.961 --> 00:18:01.294
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:01.464 --> 00:18:02.795
Naked.


00:18:03.833 --> 00:18:06.131
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:06.302 --> 00:18:07.826
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:10.273 --> 00:18:11.365
There.


00:18:11.541 --> 00:18:14.738
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:19.349 --> 00:18:20.976
I'm kidding.


00:18:21.518 --> 00:18:23.349
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:23.686 --> 00:18:24.710
No, no.


00:18:24.888 --> 00:18:28.289
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:28.458 --> 00:18:30.653
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:31.261 --> 00:18:35.925
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:36.432 --> 00:18:40.232
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:40.403 --> 00:18:42.997
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:46.876 --> 00:18:48.537
What is that?


00:18:49.112 --> 00:18:51.376
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:51.548 --> 00:18:53.516
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:54.717 --> 00:18:56.446
Hey. What...?


00:19:09.299 --> 00:19:11.790
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:11.968 --> 00:19:13.595
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:15.897
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:16.072 --> 00:19:18.336
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:18.508 --> 00:19:19.532
Do you hear this?


00:19:19.709 --> 00:19:21.370
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:21.544 --> 00:19:23.239
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:23.413 --> 00:19:25.745
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:25.915 --> 00:19:28.110
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:28.284 --> 00:19:30.149
She gave you a CD?


00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:33.687
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:34.924 --> 00:19:38.792
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:40.029 --> 00:19:44.125
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:46.102 --> 00:19:48.297
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:49.439 --> 00:19:50.997
So...


00:19:51.875 --> 00:19:54.002
...that meeting today...


00:19:54.177 --> 00:19:56.975
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:57.313 --> 00:19:59.372
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:19:59.549 --> 00:20:01.983
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:02.252 --> 00:20:03.446
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:04.921 --> 00:20:06.821
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:10.118
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:10.393 --> 00:20:14.124
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:19.035 --> 00:20:21.833
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:22.005 --> 00:20:25.065
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:25.241 --> 00:20:27.505
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:31.481 --> 00:20:33.142
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:34.817 --> 00:20:36.114
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:36.286 --> 00:20:39.380
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:39.555 --> 00:20:42.023
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:42.191 --> 00:20:44.352
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:44.527 --> 00:20:45.721
That's interesting.


00:20:45.895 --> 00:20:48.659
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:48.831 --> 00:20:50.059
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:50.233 --> 00:20:51.860
I only have cheese.


00:20:55.038 --> 00:20:57.006
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:57.173 --> 00:20:59.073
Your phone.


00:21:02.111 --> 00:21:04.978
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:05.148 --> 00:21:06.706
I have underestimated you.


00:21:07.283 --> 00:21:09.114
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:09.285 --> 00:21:12.379
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:12.555 --> 00:21:15.183
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:15.358 --> 00:21:19.556
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:19.729 --> 00:21:22.994
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:23.166 --> 00:21:26.602
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:26.769 --> 00:21:29.897
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:30.073 --> 00:21:35.204
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:36.479 --> 00:21:38.640
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:44.053 --> 00:21:48.683
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:48.858 --> 00:21:52.954
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:53.129 --> 00:21:56.895
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:57.367 --> 00:21:59.028
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:21:59.202 --> 00:22:01.363
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:04.607 --> 00:22:07.303
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:07.877 --> 00:22:11.335
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:11.781 --> 00:22:13.749
I like trouble.


00:22:15.284 --> 00:22:16.410
Hey, kids.


00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:21.156
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:21.324 --> 00:22:24.088
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:28.094
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:28.398 --> 00:22:33.631
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:33.836 --> 00:22:36.304
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:36.572 --> 00:22:39.132
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:39.308 --> 00:22:41.276
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:41.444 --> 00:22:44.504
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:47.740
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:47.917 --> 00:22:50.613
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:50.787 --> 00:22:54.086
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:54.257 --> 00:22:56.088
What if I don't want to?


00:22:57.193 --> 00:23:00.924
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:01.097 --> 00:23:03.156
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:03.332 --> 00:23:05.596
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:05.768 --> 00:23:09.329
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:09.505 --> 00:23:10.995
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:11.174 --> 00:23:12.641
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:14.243 --> 00:23:16.370
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:16.546 --> 00:23:19.674
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:20.083 --> 00:23:24.281
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:24.454 --> 00:23:28.288
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:28.458 --> 00:23:31.359
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:31.527 --> 00:23:33.791
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:33.963 --> 00:23:36.090
You are a star.


00:23:36.265 --> 00:23:40.463
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:40.636 --> 00:23:42.194
I'm a star.


00:23:42.371 --> 00:23:46.535
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:46.709 --> 00:23:49.109
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:49.278 --> 00:23:51.246
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:51.414 --> 00:23:52.972
Every part of him.


00:23:53.149 --> 00:23:56.676
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:56.853 --> 00:23:59.617
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:03.450
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:03.626 --> 00:24:05.526
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:06.129 --> 00:24:08.029
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:08.197 --> 00:24:10.893
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:11.067 --> 00:24:13.126
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:13.302 --> 00:24:14.667
Are we clear?


00:24:15.104 --> 00:24:16.298
Crystal.


00:24:18.241 --> 00:24:21.233
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:25.403
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:25.581 --> 00:24:28.049
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:28.217 --> 00:24:29.548
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:29.719 --> 00:24:31.846
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:32.021 --> 00:24:33.545
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:33.723 --> 00:24:37.090
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:39.956
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:40.129 --> 00:24:42.393
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:42.565 --> 00:24:44.123
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:44.300 --> 00:24:46.427
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:46.602 --> 00:24:48.069
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:48.237 --> 00:24:51.070
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:53.902
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:54.076 --> 00:24:55.839
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:56.012 --> 00:24:57.707
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:58.147 --> 00:25:00.843
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:01.017 --> 00:25:03.747
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:05.114
We're here to impress.


00:25:05.288 --> 00:25:07.552
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:11.394 --> 00:25:13.862
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:14.030 --> 00:25:16.294
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:16.465 --> 00:25:18.660
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:18.834 --> 00:25:22.201
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:22.371 --> 00:25:24.896
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:25.074 --> 00:25:28.339
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:28.511 --> 00:25:33.813
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:33.983 --> 00:25:40.718
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:41.924 --> 00:25:43.414
That's good.


00:25:50.466 --> 00:25:53.765
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:54.604 --> 00:25:56.936
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:57.106 --> 00:25:59.006
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:00.042 --> 00:26:03.637
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:03.813 --> 00:26:06.008
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:06.182 --> 00:26:08.116
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:08.284 --> 00:26:13.517
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:13.689 --> 00:26:15.884
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:16.425 --> 00:26:18.188
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:18.361 --> 00:26:20.955
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:21.564 --> 00:26:24.863
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:25.034 --> 00:26:26.501
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:26.669 --> 00:26:28.694
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:28.871 --> 00:26:31.863
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:34.043 --> 00:26:36.477
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:40.016 --> 00:26:41.847
Okay.


00:26:42.418 --> 00:26:44.784
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:45.121 --> 00:26:46.884
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:47.056 --> 00:26:49.047
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:49.225 --> 00:26:51.056
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:51.227 --> 00:26:53.525
That I shall not cross.


00:26:53.996 --> 00:26:56.294
So sing something.


00:26:57.967 --> 00:26:59.434
Okay.


00:27:03.572 --> 00:27:06.370
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:06.542 --> 00:27:09.033
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:09.211 --> 00:27:10.610
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:11.080 --> 00:27:13.071
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:14.884 --> 00:27:17.352
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:20.045
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:20.222 --> 00:27:21.814
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:22.325 --> 00:27:23.952
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:27.895
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:28.064 --> 00:27:30.396
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:30.566 --> 00:27:32.033
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:33.436 --> 00:27:35.097
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:36.038 --> 00:27:38.871
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:39.041 --> 00:27:44.240
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:44.413 --> 00:27:45.971
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:47.083 --> 00:27:49.677
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:49.852 --> 00:27:52.412
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:52.588 --> 00:27:56.957
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:58.361 --> 00:28:01.023
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:01.197 --> 00:28:03.461
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:03.632 --> 00:28:06.294
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:06.469 --> 00:28:08.960
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:13.442 --> 00:28:15.569
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:15.745 --> 00:28:18.373
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:18.547 --> 00:28:21.880
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:22.151 --> 00:28:24.642
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:24.820 --> 00:28:26.811
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:26.989 --> 00:28:29.287
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:29.458 --> 00:28:31.153
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:31.427 --> 00:28:33.122
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:33.562 --> 00:28:37.396
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:37.867 --> 00:28:41.963
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:42.138 --> 00:28:43.162
...good acoustics.


00:28:43.572 --> 00:28:47.406
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:47.576 --> 00:28:49.168
If you gave them your song.


00:28:50.579 --> 00:28:52.240
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:52.982 --> 00:28:55.678
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:55.851 --> 00:28:57.182
Yeah.


00:28:58.854 --> 00:29:05.384
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:05.694 --> 00:29:06.991
You wrote that song today?


00:29:07.163 --> 00:29:10.621
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:10.900 --> 00:29:12.197
You really like this guy.


00:29:12.368 --> 00:29:14.063
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:14.236 --> 00:29:16.431
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:16.605 --> 00:29:20.097
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:21.911 --> 00:29:24.709
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:28.317 --> 00:29:31.150
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:33.189 --> 00:29:35.657
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:35.991 --> 00:29:39.483
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:39.662 --> 00:29:41.687
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:41.864 --> 00:29:42.888
Am not.


00:29:43.933 --> 00:29:46.925
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:47.102 --> 00:29:49.798
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:49.972 --> 00:29:52.532
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:52.708 --> 00:29:55.404
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:55.578 --> 00:29:57.512
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:57.680 --> 00:30:01.707
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:02.084 --> 00:30:05.178
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:08.123 --> 00:30:09.647
Okay.


00:30:09.959 --> 00:30:11.551
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:11.727 --> 00:30:13.058
That's my girl.


00:30:13.329 --> 00:30:17.322
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:17.500 --> 00:30:20.799
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:20.970 --> 00:30:22.733
What? Why?


00:30:22.905 --> 00:30:24.270
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:28.177 --> 00:30:29.735
Katie!


00:30:29.912 --> 00:30:33.348
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:33.516 --> 00:30:35.006
Go.


00:30:35.184 --> 00:30:36.913
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:37.086 --> 00:30:38.417
Angie, heads up.


00:30:40.389 --> 00:30:41.686
Katie!


00:30:46.896 --> 00:30:48.625
What's going on?


00:30:48.797 --> 00:30:50.230
Nothing.


00:30:50.399 --> 00:30:53.527
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:53.702 --> 00:30:56.000
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:56.171 --> 00:31:00.232
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:03.479 --> 00:31:07.643
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:07.816 --> 00:31:10.046
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:10.219 --> 00:31:11.652
Oh, no, no.


00:31:11.820 --> 00:31:14.311
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:14.490 --> 00:31:16.788
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:16.959 --> 00:31:19.655
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:19.828 --> 00:31:20.852
Fun.


00:31:21.030 --> 00:31:24.158
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:24.333 --> 00:31:27.734
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:28.604 --> 00:31:30.629
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:34.610 --> 00:31:36.976
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:37.313 --> 00:31:39.577
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:39.882 --> 00:31:42.976
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:43.252 --> 00:31:46.415
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:46.755 --> 00:31:49.815
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:49.992 --> 00:31:52.392
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:52.561 --> 00:31:55.496
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:55.664 --> 00:31:59.691
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:31:59.969 --> 00:32:03.268
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:04.473 --> 00:32:05.770
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:15.751 --> 00:32:18.015
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:18.187 --> 00:32:20.382
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:20.990 --> 00:32:24.016
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:25.194 --> 00:32:28.322
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:29.098 --> 00:32:31.362
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:31.533 --> 00:32:33.831
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:34.003 --> 00:32:37.200
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:40.409 --> 00:32:43.037
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:43.212 --> 00:32:46.272
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:46.448 --> 00:32:49.645
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:50.552 --> 00:32:53.419
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:53.589 --> 00:32:55.648
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:55.824 --> 00:32:56.916
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:57.526 --> 00:33:00.017
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:00.195 --> 00:33:01.662
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:02.398 --> 00:33:03.729
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:03.899 --> 00:33:04.923
Mm-hm.


00:33:05.100 --> 00:33:06.499
Right.


00:33:07.503 --> 00:33:08.902
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:11.974 --> 00:33:13.236
Hmm.


00:33:18.047 --> 00:33:20.038
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:20.716 --> 00:33:21.740
Ravi?


00:33:23.419 --> 00:33:25.944
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:26.121 --> 00:33:28.555
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:30.693 --> 00:33:33.253
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:33.429 --> 00:33:34.623
Obviously.


00:33:35.164 --> 00:33:37.655
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:37.833 --> 00:33:39.391
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:39.568 --> 00:33:42.935
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:43.472 --> 00:33:46.600
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:46.775 --> 00:33:49.437
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:49.812 --> 00:33:53.213
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:53.382 --> 00:33:55.247
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:55.617 --> 00:33:57.141
But I never got my shot.


00:33:57.319 --> 00:33:59.549
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:33:59.722 --> 00:34:02.122
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:02.291 --> 00:34:04.486
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:04.660 --> 00:34:06.150
"Who is asking?"


00:34:06.428 --> 00:34:09.795
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:09.965 --> 00:34:12.559
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:12.735 --> 00:34:17.104
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:17.406 --> 00:34:19.670
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:19.842 --> 00:34:22.242
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:22.578 --> 00:34:25.206
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:25.380 --> 00:34:26.574
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:27.783 --> 00:34:30.479
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:33.288 --> 00:34:36.951
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:37.626 --> 00:34:39.685
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:39.862 --> 00:34:42.330
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:42.498 --> 00:34:43.556
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:45.134 --> 00:34:46.465
Blow it up.


00:34:48.403 --> 00:34:49.961
Thank you.


00:34:59.782 --> 00:35:01.181
Whoa.


00:35:01.350 --> 00:35:03.978
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:04.153 --> 00:35:07.213
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:08.590 --> 00:35:10.922
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:11.093 --> 00:35:14.324
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:17.032 --> 00:35:20.001
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:20.169 --> 00:35:23.798
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:24.506 --> 00:35:26.838
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:32.214 --> 00:35:33.647
Where is he?


00:35:34.483 --> 00:35:37.281
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:37.452 --> 00:35:39.113
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:39.288 --> 00:35:41.722
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:45.227 --> 00:35:48.788
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:48.964 --> 00:35:52.297
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:52.467 --> 00:35:54.662
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:54.870 --> 00:35:57.600
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:57.773 --> 00:36:00.207
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:07.015 --> 00:36:08.073
I think I found him.


00:36:08.250 --> 00:36:10.514
Well, he is blond.


00:36:13.622 --> 00:36:15.920
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:17.826 --> 00:36:20.124
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:20.295 --> 00:36:21.694
What are you doing here?


00:36:21.864 --> 00:36:24.697
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:24.867 --> 00:36:26.892
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:27.069 --> 00:36:30.004
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:30.172 --> 00:36:32.003
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:32.174 --> 00:36:34.642
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:37.079 --> 00:36:39.206
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:40.749 --> 00:36:44.185
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:44.353 --> 00:36:46.548
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:46.722 --> 00:36:49.589
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:49.758 --> 00:36:51.692
...and you're fired.


00:36:54.730 --> 00:36:58.257
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:00.869 --> 00:37:02.359
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:02.604 --> 00:37:03.730
You were amazing.


00:37:03.906 --> 00:37:04.964
Do I know you?


00:37:09.311 --> 00:37:11.905
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:14.249 --> 00:37:16.308
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:16.952 --> 00:37:19.443
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:23.959 --> 00:37:26.792
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:26.962 --> 00:37:28.327
Miss Van R.


00:37:28.964 --> 00:37:31.364
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:31.533 --> 00:37:32.727
...but were never good enough?


00:37:34.102 --> 00:37:35.763
Who told you that?


00:37:53.488 --> 00:37:54.921
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:55.090 --> 00:37:58.287
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:58.460 --> 00:37:59.586
Oh!


00:37:59.761 --> 00:38:03.993
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:08.337 --> 00:38:11.431
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:11.606 --> 00:38:14.507
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:19.281 --> 00:38:22.011
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:22.351 --> 00:38:25.047
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:25.220 --> 00:38:26.482
Follow me.


00:38:31.526 --> 00:38:33.357
Oh, wow.


00:38:35.831 --> 00:38:41.394
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:42.270 --> 00:38:44.170
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:44.339 --> 00:38:48.036
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:49.544 --> 00:38:50.738
Or not.


00:38:53.015 --> 00:38:56.041
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:02.257 --> 00:39:05.818
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:07.129 --> 00:39:11.361
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:11.533 --> 00:39:15.060
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:15.237 --> 00:39:19.230
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:21.209 --> 00:39:24.542
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:26.314 --> 00:39:30.011
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:30.685 --> 00:39:34.382
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:34.856 --> 00:39:37.689
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:38.160 --> 00:39:39.252
Uh-uh.


00:42:18.186 --> 00:42:20.780
I think I've blown something.


00:42:20.956 --> 00:42:24.016
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:26.628 --> 00:42:28.186
Move it, fatso.


00:42:29.931 --> 00:42:36.530
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:37.272 --> 00:42:40.901
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:53.455 --> 00:42:54.888
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:55.056 --> 00:42:57.081
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:57.259 --> 00:42:59.819
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:42:59.995 --> 00:43:01.963
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:04.432 --> 00:43:05.797
I'm so sorry.


00:43:06.501 --> 00:43:07.729
What...? You...?


00:43:08.436 --> 00:43:10.097
Hey. Wait.


00:43:10.272 --> 00:43:11.500
But who are you?


00:43:11.673 --> 00:43:14.267
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:22.417 --> 00:43:25.443
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:43.905 --> 00:43:45.930
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:46.708 --> 00:43:49.643
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:50.078 --> 00:43:53.013
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:53.348 --> 00:43:55.543
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:57.552 --> 00:44:00.715
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:00.889 --> 00:44:04.450
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:04.626 --> 00:44:06.890
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:07.062 --> 00:44:10.122
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:10.432 --> 00:44:13.560
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:14.469 --> 00:44:17.597
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:24.112 --> 00:44:27.343
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:27.515 --> 00:44:29.574
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:29.751 --> 00:44:31.685
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:31.853 --> 00:44:33.548
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:33.722 --> 00:44:36.020
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:37.392 --> 00:44:41.522
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:42.497 --> 00:44:46.092
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:47.168 --> 00:44:48.795
We're recording.


00:44:49.104 --> 00:44:50.935
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:51.106 --> 00:44:52.334
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:52.941 --> 00:44:54.875
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:55.043 --> 00:44:56.772
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:56.945 --> 00:44:59.277
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:44:59.447 --> 00:45:00.675
Check this out, all right?


00:45:00.849 --> 00:45:04.444
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:04.619 --> 00:45:06.450
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:06.621 --> 00:45:08.452
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:08.656 --> 00:45:10.681
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:10.859 --> 00:45:12.019
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:12.193 --> 00:45:14.161
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:14.329 --> 00:45:16.194
That was subpar at best.


00:45:16.364 --> 00:45:18.889
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:19.634 --> 00:45:22.933
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:23.104 --> 00:45:24.662
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:24.839 --> 00:45:27.205
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:27.375 --> 00:45:30.401
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:30.578 --> 00:45:33.672
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:33.848 --> 00:45:35.406
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:35.850 --> 00:45:38.717
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:39.254 --> 00:45:42.815
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:43.091 --> 00:45:46.424
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:46.594 --> 00:45:49.188
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:49.364 --> 00:45:51.832
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:52.000 --> 00:45:55.094
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:55.270 --> 00:45:57.795
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:45:59.541 --> 00:46:04.137
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:04.312 --> 00:46:07.281
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:07.449 --> 00:46:10.282
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:16.324 --> 00:46:19.521
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:38.646 --> 00:46:40.944
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:41.115 --> 00:46:42.309
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:42.484 --> 00:46:44.782
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:44.953 --> 00:46:46.318
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:47.155 --> 00:46:49.282
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:49.457 --> 00:46:50.583
This is not good.


00:46:52.160 --> 00:46:53.957
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:54.128 --> 00:46:55.959
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:56.130 --> 00:46:58.530
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:58.700 --> 00:47:02.136
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:02.303 --> 00:47:03.327
Listen...


00:47:03.505 --> 00:47:06.941
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:07.108 --> 00:47:08.769
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:20.622 --> 00:47:24.615
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:24.792 --> 00:47:27.784
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:27.962 --> 00:47:31.591
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:31.766 --> 00:47:35.702
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:35.870 --> 00:47:39.670
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:40.208 --> 00:47:43.109
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:43.278 --> 00:47:46.338
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:48.149 --> 00:47:50.083
It was you?


00:47:50.752 --> 00:47:53.846
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:54.789 --> 00:47:58.623
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:00.261 --> 00:48:03.287
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:03.464 --> 00:48:06.228
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:06.401 --> 00:48:08.528
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:09.170 --> 00:48:11.900
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:12.173 --> 00:48:13.936
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:14.108 --> 00:48:17.475
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:17.645 --> 00:48:19.909
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:21.416 --> 00:48:23.213
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:23.384 --> 00:48:24.476
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:25.420 --> 00:48:26.887
You have a date with detention.


00:48:27.055 --> 00:48:28.522
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:28.690 --> 00:48:30.419
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:30.592 --> 00:48:33.288
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:33.461 --> 00:48:36.589
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:36.764 --> 00:48:38.254
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:38.433 --> 00:48:40.333
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:40.501 --> 00:48:43.299
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:43.471 --> 00:48:45.837
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:46.007 --> 00:48:47.474
Fine.


00:48:48.276 --> 00:48:49.800
I hate you.


00:48:53.448 --> 00:48:57.578
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:57.852 --> 00:48:59.786
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:06.361 --> 00:49:07.988
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:08.162 --> 00:49:11.359
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:11.532 --> 00:49:12.999
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:13.167 --> 00:49:15.965
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:16.137 --> 00:49:18.332
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


